      "content": "I'm glad you're monitoring your symptoms, but it's important to stick with your prescribed dose of lisinopril. Dizziness and lightheadedness can sometimes result from sudden changes in blood pressure, especially when standing up. However, this can usually be managed by taking your medication with meals and standing up slowly. Getting a double dosage isn't recommended and should be avoided, as it can increase the risk of worsening your condition. If your symptoms persist or worsen, please contact your doctor for advice.",
